    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling offensive output today, anchored by a trio of elite-tier starts. **Yordan Alvarez** (82.97) leads the charge with an elite xwOBA of 0.471 against a generous 4.97 xERA arm, and while his lineup position is pending, his projected #2 spot makes him our primary anchor. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) follows closely as our most efficient play for stolen base upside; he benefits from a highly favorable matchup against a 5.16 xERA pitcher, compounded by a wind-aided park boost that pushed his daily score well into elite territory. Additionally, **Trea Turner** (79.40) and **Kyle Schwarber** (78.21) offer massive value atop the order against Bieber, whose 5.23 xERA provides a target-rich environment for our top-of-the-order speed and power threats.\n\nWhile these core players thrive, we are exercising caution with several middle-of-the-pack options. **Junior Caminero** (59.32) remains a strong start despite a pedestrian park environment, largely carried by his favorable xwOBA. Conversely, **Dillon Dingler** (40.50) barely cleared our starting threshold; the drop-off is driven by a disadvantageous platoon matchup against Logan Webb, which significantly stifled his raw projection. The most difficult personnel decision involved **Josh Smith** (32.43), who sits on the bench today primarily due to a brutal platoon disadvantage against a sub-3.20 xERA pitcher and a suboptimal #8 spot in the order. Despite his utility, **Josh Smith** failed to meet our 40.0 efficiency floor, leading us to favor the better situational alignment of our active starters. We remain fully monitored for potential lineup shifts regarding **Yordan Alvarez** or late-scratch risks, but the roster as constructed is optimized for category-wide efficiency.",
